# NOTE: /public/build is intentionally NOT ignored (deviates from the
# Laravel default). The production server does have Node.js, so building
# there is possible — but deploys are driven by hand through the Plesk UI
# with no deployment actions wired up, and building server-side then means
# the site 500s (no manifest.json) for the whole gap between "Pull Now" and
# the npm run build that follows it. Committing the compiled Vite output
# keeps a deploy to pull + clear caches, with no broken window. The cost is
# that every frontend change must be rebuilt and recommitted from a dev
# machine. Revisit if Plesk deployment actions ever run the build for us.
/public/storage
/storage/*.key
/storage/pail
/vendor

# dompdf's font cache (config/dompdf.php font_dir/font_cache). Regenerated
# automatically the first time a PDF is exported. Also, on this project it
# currently caches a copy of Tahoma (see app/Console/Commands/RegisterPdfThaiFont.php)
# which is a Windows-bundled font and not freely redistributable — must
# never be committed regardless of the "just a cache" reason above.
/storage/fonts
Homestead.json
Homestead.yaml
Thumbs.db
